From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:57:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tests/color-management: Cover signed custom primaries end to
 end

Add regressions for the custom-primaries input path:

 - /wayland/custom-primaries/negative-coordinate: the test client sends
   ACES AP0, an encoding gamut whose blue primary has y = -0.077, through
   set_primaries, sets it on a surface and commits. The compositor side
   checks the surface's retained ClutterColorState holds the requested
   coordinates (negative, unclamped) and that the matrices the color
   transform renders with map test colors to linear BT.2020 as an
   independent double-precision reference computes them (RGB->XYZ,
   Bradford to D65, XYZ->BT.2020), and back.
 - /wayland/custom-primaries/unsupported: collinear primaries, nearly
   collinear primaries (with the white point inside and outside the
   sliver they span), a white point with y = 0, with y < 0 and outside
   the primaries' triangle, and a coordinate beyond 16 each produce an
   image description that fails with the 'unsupported' cause, while a
   large imaginary gamut at the 16 limit is accepted; the connection
   survives and a following valid description is applied to the surface.
 - /wayland/custom-primaries/info-round-trip: an output description with
   the same AP0 primaries (driven through the synthetic output's native
   SDR mode) reports every coordinate, including the negative one,
   exactly in the image description information event. It rewrites the
   fixture output, so it runs as a separate invocation.
